%T A397814 785986132795927,1085288377801424865,2992747331862253111047
%N A397814 Number of nonisomorphic directed acyclic graphs (DAGs) on n vertices with trivial automorphism group.
%C A397814 A DAG is asymmetric if its automorphism group is trivial.
%D A397814 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, New York, 1973, pp. 191-194.
%D A397814 R. W. Robinson, Counting unlabeled acyclic digraphs, Combinatorial Mathematics V, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 622 (1977), 28-43.
%H A397814 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A397814/a397814.pdf">Asymmetric directed acyclic graphs</a>.
%F A397814 F(H) = Sum_{K >= H} E(K), hence E(H) = Sum_{K >= H} mu(H,K)*F(K). For DAGs, F(H) is computed by inclusion-exclusion over the nonempty H-invariant sets of sources, with the arcs from the source set to its complement chosen as unions of H-orbits. a(n) = E({1})/n!.
%e A397814 For n=4, there are 17 nonisomorphic asymmetric DAGs; they are illustrated in the linked accompanying note. Hence a(4) = 17.
%K A397814 nonn,hard,more,new
